{% set name = "Universal Resolver" %}
{% set logo = "sketching" %}
{% set subtitle = "Community DID Infrastructure" %}
{% set repoTag = "" %}

{% extends "default.html.njk" %}
<!-- {% block svg %}

{% endblock %} -->

{% block content %}
  <section class="page-title theme-bg">
    <div class="container">
      <svg>
        <use xlink:href="/images/icons.svg#{{ logo }}"></use>
      </svg>
      <h1>{{ name }}</h1>
      {% if subtitle %}
        <h3>{{ subtitle }}</h3>
      {% else %}
        <h3>Decentralized Identity Foundation</h3>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="counter-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row justify-content-md-center">
        <div class="col-6">
          <div class="section-title text-center">
            <h2 class="font-alt">A Successful Incubation</h2>
            <div class="title-border">
              <span class="lg"></span>
              <span class="md"></span>
              <span class="sm"></span>
            </div>
            <br>
            <p>
              As of October 14, 2026, The Decentralized Identity Foundation is no longer hosting a "community staging 
              server" for the Universal Resolver. The complexity of hosting and administering it as a public resource has 
              grown over the years, and the number of production-grade implementations of the Universal Resolver specification 
              (with free tiers) have largely obviated the need for DIF to "seed" the market, which is growing into 
              maturity.
            </p>
            <p>
              Developers who were using DIF's community resolver (which was powered, all along, by GoDiddy's staging backend) 
              are encouraged to consider using one of the two resolvers listed below for experimentation and research, and to 
              consider DIF-affiliated commercial options for production infrastructural needs. Both deployments are 
              deployed and funded by DIF members, who maintain the respective reference implementations they are based on through
              DIF, including change requests, bug fixes, and ongoing review of new drivers, whether dockerized, NPM-packaged, or 
              both. Some of these drivers, like those for 
              <a href=https://github.com/decentralized-identity/ethr-did-resolver><code>did:ethr</code></a> and 
              <a href=https://github.com/decentralized-identity/uni-resolver-driver-did-webvh><code>did:webvh</code></a>
              are, in turn, also DIF work items, and thus good examples to analyze if you are planning your own driver contribution.
           </p>
           <p>
             In historical order, the main DIF-member deployments are:
           </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

<section class="counter-section gray-bg">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row justify-content-md-center">
        <div class="col-3">
          <div class="section-title text-center">
            <h2 class="font-alt">GoDiddy, by DanubeTech</h2>
            <p>
              <i>Productionized reference implementation of the original Universal Resolver form-factor.</i>
            </p>
            <div class="title-border">
              <span class="lg"></span>
              <span class="md"></span>
              <span class="sm"></span>
            </div>
            <br>
            <p>
            <a href="https://godiddy.com/app/resolve">GoDiddy's production front-end</a>, which continues to run DanubeTech's
             foundational reference implementation of the specification they 
             <a href="https://github.com/decentralized-identity/universal-resolver">donated to DIF</a> and managed here.
             It is comprised of a workhorse Java router and docker containers per method to support the widest possible range of resolution designs.
             </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-3">
          <div class="section-title text-center">
            <h2 class="font-alt">ThisDID, by GoPlausible</h2>
            <p>
              <i>Edge-worker-optimized and proxy-fallback wrapper around DIF's NPM-based resolver engine</i>
            </p>
            <div class="title-border">
              <span class="lg"></span>
              <span class="md"></span>
              <span class="sm"></span>
            </div>
            <br>
            <p>
            <a href="https://thisdid.com">ThisDID.com</a>, is a more recent re-architecting of the Veramo-project-maintained
            <a href="https://github.com/decentralized-identity/did-resolver">TypeScript/NPM reference implementation</a>. It uses 
            an edge-worker deployment to route and proxy resolution to optimize for low latency and operational cost for methods
            which have been packaged as NPM packages, and has a "fallback" to proxied resolution everywhere else, load-balancing
            (and ranking) where multiple backends support these non-NPM resolution drivers.
             </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Blog End -->
{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}
  {{ super() }}
  <script src="/js/education.js"></script>
{% endblock %}